sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User or visitor
    actor AD as Admin
    participant A as Express API
    participant M as MongoDB

    rect rgb(240, 246, 252)
    Note over U,M: Report incorrect data (UC-09)
    U->>A: POST /api/tors/:id/report (description, optional email)
    A->>M: check the TOR exists
    A->>M: create ErrorReport (status open, reportedBy or reporterEmail)
    A-->>U: 201
    end

    rect rgb(245, 240, 252)
    Note over AD,M: Review the queue (UC-26, UC-28)
    AD->>A: GET /api/admin/tors/reported
    A->>A: requireAuth, role admin, 2FA verified
    A->>M: group open ErrorReports by TOR, newest first
    A-->>AD: one row per TOR with open count and latest report
    AD->>A: GET /api/admin/tors/:id
    AD->>A: GET /api/admin/reports?status=open&torId=:id
    A-->>AD: the TOR and its open reports
    opt open the AI flag details (FR-19)
        AD->>A: GET /api/admin/tors/:id/fairness-flags
        A->>M: read flags with reasoning and data points
        A-->>AD: flags
    end
    end

    rect rgb(240, 250, 244)
    Note over AD,M: Correct the TOR and resolve the reports (UC-27, FR-40)
    AD->>A: PATCH /api/admin/tors/:id (fields, resolveFlags, resolveReports, resolutionNote)
    A->>A: validate with zod
    A->>M: update the TOR fields
    opt resolveReports
        A->>M: mark every open report on the TOR resolved (admin, time, note)
    end
    A->>M: write SystemLog (what changed)
    A->>A: log the admin action (who, route, outcome) to the application log
    A-->>AD: 200 with the updated TOR
    end

    Note over U,A: The reporter later sees the resolution in GET /api/auth/reports
